---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Growth" description="Let's find the big problem you're actually solving.">
  <section class="hero-small">
    <span class="tenet-label">Core Tenet</span>
    <h1>"We're doing fine but <span class="highlight">should be doing better</span>"</h1>
    <p class="hero-answer">You're right. Let's find the big problem you're actually solving.</p>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The Problem</h2>
    <div class="problem-text">
      <p>
        You're not in crisis. Revenue is okay. Team is stable. But you have this nagging feeling 
        that you're leaving opportunity on the table.
      </p>
      <p>
        The issue isn't execution. It's focus. You're trying to be everything to everyone 
        instead of being the obvious choice for someone specific.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">How I Help</h2>
    <div class="approach">
      <div class="approach-item">
        <h3>Find Your Highest Priority Problem</h3>
        <p>Through deep research with customers and colleagues, I identify the biggest, most profitable problem you're uniquely positioned to solve.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-item">
        <h3>Align Everyone Around It</h3>
        <p>Growth stalls when different teams are solving different problems. I create the narrative that unites sales, product, marketing, and leadership.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-item">
        <h3>Build the Proof</h3>
        <p>Vision without evidence is just hope. I help you create the case studies, data, and demonstrations that make your value undeniable.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-label">The Framework</h2>
    <div class="framework">
      <p>This approach is based on my <strong>Storyselling</strong> methodology, documented in my book <em>Solved to Sold</em>.</p>
      <p>The core idea: clients want solutions, not products. The businesses that win are the ones who've identified their Highest Priority Problem and built everything around solving it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <h2>Ready to find your focus?</h2>
    <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com" class="cta-button">Let's Talk</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-small {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  
  .tenet-label {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .hero-small h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  
  .hero-answer {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  
  .problem-text p {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  
  .approach {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  
  .approach-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    background: #111;
  }
  
  .approach-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .approach-item p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .framework {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  
  .framework p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .framework strong {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .framework em {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  
  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
